{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (runtime-proven). Reproduced the no-op churn in isolation: a two-pass runtime probe recorded the SAME authoritative link (LOC-1|LOC-2|blocks, identical link_id/direction/source) across two passes; the on-disk sidecar hash differed between passes (7d849e3… vs 58fba08…) solely because 'confirmed_at' (time.time_ns) and 'confirmed_pass' refreshed. Mechanism: PeerConfirmationStore.record() rebuilds the record every call and sets _dirty=True UNCONDITIONALLY (peer_confirmations.py:142-173); save() then rewrites the full JSON sidecar whenever _dirty (:175-189). Nothing gates the write on a MATERIAL change.\n\nAuthority / defect class: this is the 'no-op bridge-state churn' class epic 0303 already governs. peer_state.py codifies 0303's discipline explicitly — bridge-state fields must be 'fixed size, change-gated, never a per-pass timestamp' (peer_state.py rich-emit section; note_rich_emit is change-gated in both directions and a no-op pass writes zero entries). confirmed_at/confirmed_pass are exactly the per-pass timestamps that discipline forbids, so this is a defect, not a design gap.\n\nConsumer contract: repository-wide search finds NO production reader of confirmed_pass or confirmed_at outside the writer; only unit tests assert them (test_peer_confirmations_store.py:162,398; _backfill.py:75; _snapshot.py:91,218-219). is_confirmed()/get() — the safety-critical readers — key only on record EXISTENCE and first_confirmed_at, never on the volatile pair. So the pair is removable telemetry, not a supported audit contract.\n\nDefect origin: the per-pass-timestamp record shape was introduced by nonlineal-melancholy-grouper (248f-ac00-18db-4259, 'Persist a peer-confirmation record per managed link'); it is amplified to every-pass churn by soured-elmy-ostrich (83d3-61d9-fc59-424b, 'Confirm links from authoritative fetched snapshots'), which re-record()s every observed link each pass. caused_by = 248f-ac00-18db-4259.\n\nFix direction (matches the ticket plan + 0303): remove the volatile confirmed_pass/confirmed_at fields (deliberate removal — no production consumer) and make record() change-gated so an unchanged link leaves _dirty false and save() writes nothing. Keep first_confirmed_at (set-once durable provenance) and all identity/decision fields, preserving relation-scoped, monotonic, additive, fail-open confirmation. One-time bounded migration: the first time each pre-existing record is re-observed post-upgrade its stored shape is rewritten once (dropping the two keys), after which unchanged passes converge to zero writes."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787552686173468001,"uuid":"c625d25f-cf32-48f5-8830-b8b18878f58a"}